{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:52.080063+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hi @wsmoses thanks for the issue.\n\nCurrently while-loop command buffer is not supported in hipgraph/hipruntime yet, it's best to disable command buffer on ROCm side.\n\n","created_at":"2026-08-10T09:16:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/46952#issuecomment-5238221835","id":5238221835,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABODjsCw","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5238221835/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-08-10T09:20:16Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5238221835","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913790?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/i-chaochen","id":913790,"login":"i-chaochen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzc5MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> Is there a known interaction between hipGraphExec replay and HSA queue interception on this ROCm version? If this reproduces on your side, the fix likely belongs in ROCm/HSA or rocprofiler — but XLA is the component that can detect it.\n\nYes, there are some know issues on previous ROCm version about rocprof-sdk + HSA hipruntime, it's best to use our CI docker image, rocm7.2.4\n\n> Consider gating command buffers off by default (or behind a version check) for ROCm stacks where graph replay is known to fault: a time-stepping loop is precisely the shape command buffers accelerate, so users on affected stacks currently trade a deterministic first-step crash for the feature's default-on setting.\n\nSeems you're referring a specific while loop sceanrio that ideally for dynamic control flow in cudagraph/hipgraph with conditonal nodes, if you have that hlo dump out, we're happy to look it how we can optimise.\n","created_at":"2026-08-10T09:30:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/46952#issuecomment-5238375465","id":5238375465,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABODtEKQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5238375465/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-08-10T11:27:05Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5238375465","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913790?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/i-chaochen","id":913790,"login":"i-chaochen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzc5MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913790?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/i-chaochen","id":913790,"login":"i-chaochen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzc5MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913790?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/i-chaochen","id":913790,"login":"i-chaochen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzc5MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-chaochen","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Summary\n\nOn AMD Instinct `gfx950:sramecc+:xnack-` (ROCm 7.1.25442), the **first execution** of a compiled XLA:GPU program whose time-stepping while-loop body was packaged into a command buffer segfaults inside the HSA runtime while launching the HIP graph. Compilation and all preceding executions of non-command-buffer programs succeed; the same computation runs correctly when the thunks are executed directly (`--xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer=`), so the fault is confined to graph *replay*, not to any kernel in the program.\n\nOriginally diagnosed by @ftynse while bringing an Oceananigans (ocean-simulation) adjoint up on MI350 through [Reactant.jl](https://github.com/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl), which embeds XLA via PJRT — full findings write-up [here](https://gist.github.com/ftynse/5c3816a1cea5daa7dc189b937b62f9ca) (issue 6). Filing on their behalf; hardware access for follow-up experiments is theirs, not mine.\n\n## Environment\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| GPU | AMD Instinct, `gfx950:sramecc+:xnack-` |\n| ROCm (driver / runtime / toolkit) | 7.1.25442 |\n| XLA | statically linked into Reactant's `libReactantExtra` (jll 0.0.404; current pin `841f8d2d5c9e340a998dda6690dec6e1b0b29e9b` via JAX's revision.bzl) |\n| Host | Julia 1.11.9 process, PJRT `StreamExecutorGpuClient` |\n| Also present | `librocprofiler64` HSA queue interceptor (see below) |\n\n## Stack at the fault\n\n```\nrocr::core::InterceptQueue::Submit                     (libhsa-runtime64.so.1)\nrocr::HSA::hsa_signal_store_screlease                  (libhsa-runtime64.so.1)\nrocprofiler::hip::hip_api_impl<…hipGraphExec…>         (librocprofiler64.so)\nstream_executor::gpu::RocmCommandBuffer::LaunchGraph   (libReactantExtra.so)\nstream_executor::gpu::GpuCommandBuffer::Submit\nxla::gpu::CommandBufferThunk::ExecuteOnStream\nxla::gpu::WhileThunk::ExecuteOnStream\n```\n\nThe `hipGraphLaunch` never returns an error code XLA could surface — the process dies inside `hsa_signal_store_screlease` under the profiler's queue interception, so there is no status for `RocmCommandBuffer::LaunchGraph` to check.\n\n## What is established\n\n- **Deterministic** on this stack: the run crashes at the first executed step (`warmup`), every time, after `compile` and non-graph executions have all succeeded.\n- **Confined to the command-buffer path**: an identical configuration with `--xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer=` (the empty set — XLA's own escape hatch, quoted verbatim in XLA's error text for a different command-buffer failure mode) completes and produces correct results. A/B evidence is in the gist (`smoke08` crash vs `smoke09` ok).\n- **Not isolated**: the `rocprofiler` frames indicate an HSA queue interceptor is installed, which may or may not be a necessary ingredient — that has not been separated yet. The three-way boundary (ROCm HSA / rocprofiler / XLA `RocmCommandBuffer`) is exactly why this is being reported with the full stack rather than bounced between components.\n\n## Suggested minimal reproducer (not yet built)\n\nAn XLA-level `while` loop of small kernels executed under a command buffer on gfx950 with ROCm 7.1.25442 — i.e. the shape `CommandBufferThunk` produces for `WhileThunk` bodies — once with and once without `librocprofiler64` loaded, to split the interceptor question.\n\n## Asks\n\n1. Is there a known interaction between `hipGraphExec` replay and HSA queue interception on this ROCm version? If this reproduces on your side, the fix likely belongs in ROCm/HSA or rocprofiler — but XLA is the component that can *detect* it.\n2. Consider gating command buffers off by default (or behind a version check) for ROCm stacks where graph replay is known to fault: a time-stepping loop is precisely the shape command buffers accelerate, so users on affected stacks currently trade a deterministic first-step crash for the feature's default-on setting.\n\nHappy to relay follow-up experiments to the original reporter, who has the hardware.","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/comments","created_at":"2026-08-09T07:12:07Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/46952","id":5101356896,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"D87D2C","default":false,"description":"Awaiting response from contributor/author","id":8177914347,"name":"stat:awaiting response from contributor","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAAB53ER6w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/stat:awaiting%20response%20from%20contributor"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABMBCHYA","number":46952,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/timeline","title":"[ROCm] SIGSEGV in HSA InterceptQueue when replaying a while-loop command buffer as a HIP graph (gfx950)","type":null,"updated_at":"2026-08-13T04:26:12Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1260124?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wsmoses","id":1260124,"login":"wsmoses","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjAxMjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses","user_view_type":"public"}},"pages":{"comments":[{"page":1,"records":2,"sha256":"3f436a0cbc9c367f78a754a147f8fffd2c13a74b59b5d2393fa1027b61912ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/comments?per_page=100&page=1"}],"issue":[{"etag":"\"ead65d821c4413d18231b05e50c129141fdc243d16de8c2bd8aa063eb1fb23ad\"","last_modified":"Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:12:53 GMT","records":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952"}],"timeline":[{"page":1,"records":10,"sha256":"8fc015cd38f903aa1b4d055204ad932792652a5856b8de98944f26177e632829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/46952/timeline?per_page=100&page=1"}]},"record_id":"github-openxla-xla-46952","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/46952","timeline":[{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1512299?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ftynse","id":1512299,"login":"ftynse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTIyOTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09T07:12:09Z","event":"mentioned","id":29176738435,"node_id":"MEE_lADOHyx1PM8AAAABMBCHYM8AAAAGyxGygw","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/events/29176738435"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1512299?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ftynse","id":1512299,"login":"ftynse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTIyOTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ftynse","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09T07:12:09Z","event":"subscribed","id":29176738454,"node_id":"SE_lADOHyx1PM8AAAABMBCHYM8AAAAGyxGylg","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/events/29176738454"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1260124?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wsmoses","id":1260124,"login":"wsmoses","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjAxMjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wsmoses","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-08-09T07:12:15Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Mitigates issue 6 of @ftynse's [ROCm findings](https://gist.github.com/ftynse/5c3816a1cea5daa7dc189b937b62f9ca): `SIGSEGV` in `rocr::core::InterceptQueue::Submit` → `RocmCommandBuffer::LaunchGraph` on the first execution of a while-loop command buffer, on gfx950 / ROCm 7.1 — deterministic, after compile/spinup succeeded, and gone entirely with command buffers off (their `smoke08` vs `smoke09` runs).\n\n## Change\n\n`XLA.get_debug_options` / `make_compile_options` now take the client's `platform`; on `\"rocm\"` the `xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer` list is cleared — the per-compile equivalent of XLA's own documented escape hatch `--xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer=`. Both compile paths (PJRT `compile_mlir!` and the IFRT resharding path) pass the platform through.\n\nThe override ordering keeps this a *default*, not a lock-out: user kwargs are applied after, so `xla_debug_options=(; xla_gpu_enable_command_buffer=[...])` re-enables them — the right knob for testing whether a newer ROCm stack still crashes.\n\n## Cost\n\nReal and worth stating: a time-stepping loop is many small kernels, exactly the shape command buffers accelerate — disabling them pays full per-launch overhead every iteration. But a deterministic crash on the first executed step costs more, and the flag flip back is one line once the HSA/rocprofiler/XLA interaction is isolated upstream.\n\n## Verification\n\nUnit-checked on CUDA hardware (no AMD GPU available locally): `platform=\"rocm\"` produces an empty command-buffer list, `platform=\"cuda\"` keeps XLA's defaults (CONDITIONAL, CUBLAS, …, FUSION), an explicit user override wins over the ROCm default, and an end-to-end `@jit` compile on CUDA is unaffected.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015drPT8jCwS74HnX6vEBCxz","closed_at":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/issues/3175/comments","created_at":"2026-08-09T06:51:35Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/issues/3175/events","html_url":"https://github.com/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/pull/3175","id":5101292113,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/issues/3175/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLq0JDM78krMw","number":3175,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/pull/3175.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/EnzymeAD/Reactant.jl/pull/3175","merged_